<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 98-day T-bills 39.5 pct sold,yield 88 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 98-day T-bills 39.5 pct sold,yield 88 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry offer of 4.8 billion levs of 98-day floater coupon T-bills was 39.48 percent sold, yielding 88.30 percent until maturity, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered on Friday with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at 20 percent monthly or 240 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		    BG 3019996027</p>
<p> Par value			 4.8 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		    October 25, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date			October 31, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date		   February 6, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		   4,800 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	     72.61 levs</p>
<p> Bids approved		   1,895 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	    87.33 levs</p>
<p> Average yield to maturity   88.30 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
